NAVER Corporation has modified all three files.  The audio HAL runs in
HIDL passthrough mode on WhaleOS: the 64-bit audioserver dlopens our
64-bit CRAS HAL directly, because the hwbinder audio service is 32-bit
and cannot load a 64-bit shared object.  The overrides make the
container's init configuration match that.

  audioserver.rc
      All vendor.audio-hal-* triggers removed - with the HAL loaded in
      process, a separate HAL service can never register with
      hwservicemanager and only crash-loops.  Two WhaleOS-specific
      actions added: an early-boot fixup that prepends libfmq.so,
      libmedia_helper.so and libaudioutils.so to the sphal->vndk link in
      /linkerconfig/ld.config.txt, and a belt-and-suspenders stop of
      vendor.audio-hal on boot.  Everything else is identical to the
      file in the image.

  android.hardware.audio.service.rc
      "disabled" added so class_start hal does not launch the service,
      and the onrestart entry that restarts audioserver when the HAL
      crashes removed.

  manifest.xml
      The android.hardware.audio HAL entry declares
      <transport arch="64">passthrough</transport> instead of hwbinder.

